        "date_published": "2026-11-18T01:28:33+00:00",
        "description": "In recent years, Pinglu County in Yuncheng, Shanxi Province, has stepped up its efforts to protect the local environment, making the most of its unique location in the Shanxi-Shaanxi-Henan region along the Yellow River and its 6,691.2 hectares of Yellow River wetlands. As a result, the Sanwan Yellow River Wetland has become an important wintering ground for rare bird species, including Whooper Swans. More than 2,000 Whooper Swans are now spending the winter at Sanwan, with numbers expected to peak at the end of November. Across the county, the total is expected to exceed 10,000. The wetland has also become a habitat for other bird species, including Falcated Ducks, black storks and egrets. Known as China's \"Hometown of Whooper Swans\", Pinglu is one of the country's most important habitats for Whooper Swans and other rare birds. Through a range of conservation efforts, local residents are helping create a thriving environment where people and nature live in harmony. (Recorded)",
